<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n36683" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξᾰμάω</span></b>  (A), <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>mow or reap out, finish mowing</i> or <i>reaping,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξαμᾷ θέρος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pers.</u>
					822
				</span></i>
			, cf.<i><span class="en">
				<u>Ag.</u>
				1655
			</span></i> (troch.), <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Ba.</u>
				1315
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σπείρων . . κἀξαμῶν
			ἅπαξ</span> sowing and <i>reaping,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Tr.</u>
				33
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χρυσοῦν θέρος ἐξαμησάμενος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Demetr.</u>
					4
				</span></i>
			:—
				Pass.
			, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γένους ἅπαντος ῥίζαν
				ἐξημημένος</span> (pf.
			part.) <i>having</i> all the race <i>cut off</i>
			root and branch, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Aj.</u>
				1178
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Paus.
				8.7.7
			</span></i>.—Poet. and later Prose. [On the quantity, 
				v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμάω.]</span>
			 (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξαμοῦν: ἐκθερίζειν</span> is
			corrupt in <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>)</div>
